Level	Description
-----	------------------------------------------------
100	CSIM init routines
101	memory settings
102	buffer settings
105	SST commands (nop,swap,fastfill,triangle+#)
106	statistics after SwapBuffers
110	sstDownLoadTexture
120	SET/GET macros
121	PCI reads/writes
122	Verilog PCI reads/writes
125	opcode+status+modes
125	registers before GO
126	SST command parameter info
127	triangle setup info
128	triangle setup vertex info
130	registers after GO
131	LFB accesses
132	LFB data
133	registers before each span within commands
134	pixel x,y and count
135	internal RGBA/STW span regs per pixel
136	push,pop operations
136	internal span loop control
137	line stipple iteration
138	X look-ahead optimizations
139	Y look-ahead optimizations
140	FBI input rgba
141	FBI input zw
142	rgba after texture modulation
143	fog computation (per new scanline)
144	rgba after fog
145	rgba after alpha blend
146	start/end antialias coverages
149	rgba after dither/truncate
150	put_pixel[x,y] (except for GLide)
155	get_pixel[x,y]
160	pixel failed rect-clipped or stipple test
161	pixel failed chromakeyed test
162	pixel failed zfunction test
163	pixel failed alphafunc test
165	RGBAZ clamping
168	fbiPixelsIn
169	fbiPixelsOut
170	texture u,v coords
171	RGBA into TREX
172	texture RGBA
173	RGB out of TREX
174	palette translations
175	lod computations
176	NCC translations
177	bilinear blending
178	TREX chromakey
190	texture memory writes
191	 details
195	texture tracing
198	memory writes
199	memory reads
300	init random screen
301	memory writes during init random screen


HINT - use levels in 140-169 for fbi , 170-199 for trex
TODO - swap TREX and FBI levels? since TREX occurs first

set SST_STATS=1	 : display pixel counter stats every swap
set SST_STATS=-1 : display stats every swap, and then reset counters
NOTE: GDBG_LEVEL must be >= 106 to get display of stats
